{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
When [Am]Israel was in Egypt's land,
[E7]Let my [Am]people go;
Op[Am]pressed so hard they could not stand,
[E7]Let my [Am]people go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Go down, [Dm]Moses,
[E7]Way down in [Am]Egypt's land;
[Am]Tell old [Dm]Pharaoh
To [E7]let my [Am]people go.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
"Thus [Am]saith the Lord," bold Moses said,
"[E7]Let my [Am]people go;
If [Am]not I'll smite your first-born dead,
[E7]Let my [Am]people go."
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
No [Am]more shall they in bondage toil,
[E7]Let my [Am]people go;
Let [Am]them come out with Egypt's spoil,
[E7]Let my [Am]people go.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Am}
